      "closure_rationale": "The actual retained OwPin address/pending/logical-owner protocol is distinguished from native pthread identity, callback notification and terminal reclamation. A copied self-referential record is diagnosed by comparing two actual live objects without dangling dereference. Previously inspected Rust Pin passages remain a bounded comparison; C pointers, public fields and caller-supplied numbers cannot enforce the whole lifetime protocol. The adapter actually composes FAsync f_submit/cancel/complete from canonical io.async PR-T21-02 with OwPin, reserving terminal counter headroom and publishing state/output transactionally. Notification stores a result without clearing pending. The real pthread adapter checks owner identity and joins the worker after its foreign receiver returns, before completing the core, rebinding or releasing actual OwAllocator backing. A callback or done flag alone does not authorize reuse. Six C17 profiles execute seven anchors, eight compiled controls and seven compiling-stub semantic rejections. An independent event specification checks37449histories of length0..5 with full state and output canaries; separate tests reach final generation/release counters. Eight controls distinguish timeout, notification, completion identity, reserved cleanup capacity, actual retained pin checks and both adapter/Pd quiescence gates. Actual object imports, stack/code sizes and seven same-contract timing samples are retained; finite traces and sanitizer observations do not prove arbitrary schedules or pointer lifetimes. The foreign-executor variant runs actual pthreads and holds the receiver before callback return, observing pending/recovery/no-release despite notification; actual join precedes reuse. Separate GCC/Clang C17 TSan runs are diagnostic-clean for these executions. The delayed device adapter imports the actual PR-T28-06 Pd provider through an exact public header/unfinished stub, and original RAM callbacks write after timeout and EN clear while FIFO remains nonempty. Matching token/disabled/FIFO-empty/TC plus actual Pd finalize is required; error results separate guaranteed complete from possibly written bytes. Exported native composition selects the exact external provider, rejects its absence and rejects the compiling unfinished provider semantically. This is implemented author support and a physical evidence protocol, not a physical DMA observation; dedicated device validation remains not run. Bounded author support only."
    },
